{"data": {"results": [{"index": 1, "use_case": "Make a new label called ProjectX in my inbox.", "execution_guidance": "IMPORTANT: Follow the recommended plan below. Extract steps before execution, adapt to your current context, execute sequentially with current_step parameter, and check known pitfalls to avoid errors.", "recommended_plan_steps": ["[Required] [Prerequisite]: Check for an existing user-created label using GMAIL_LIST_LABELS (match exact labels[].name; ignore labels[].type='system'; build name→id map).", "[Required (if no matching user label exists)] [Step]: Create the label using GMAIL_CREATE_LABEL (support hierarchy via '/' in the label name; persist returned data.id as canonical, including any returned color values).", "[Optional (if visibility/color/name must change)] [Next Step]: Modify mutable properties using GMAIL_UPDATE_LABEL (user labels only; target by label id, not display name).", "[Required] [Next Step]: Confirm canonical id + properties using GMAIL_GET_LABEL (by id) or re-run GMAIL_LIST_LABELS (ensure it appears as a user label).", "[Optional (if rollback is approved)] [Next Step]: Remove the label definition using GMAIL_DELETE_LABEL (by label id).", "[Optional (if HTTP 409 conflict, HTTP 500 backendError, or HTTP 400 validation/FAILED_PRECONDITION)] [Fallback]: Re-check state via GMAIL_LIST_LABELS or GMAIL_GET_LABEL, simplify/adjust label name and/or accepted colors, then retry GMAIL_CREATE_LABEL or GMAIL_UPDATE_LABEL with brief backoff."], "known_pitfalls": ["[GMAIL_LIST_LABELS] Response can be wrapped/offloaded in some runtimes—ensure you extract the full data.labels array before concluding a label is missing.", "[GMAIL_CREATE_LABEL] Duplicate/conflict may surface as HTTP 409 and new labels may not be immediately readable; rely on returned data.id and retry reads after a short delay.", "[GMAIL_CREATE_LABEL] HTTP 400 can occur if background/text colors are not in Gmail’s accepted palette; treat returned colors as canonical (may differ from requested).", "[GMAIL_CREATE_LABEL] HTTP 400 status='FAILED_PRECONDITION' or other validation errors can occur for certain names/hierarchy paths or disallowed characters; retry with a simpler label name.", "[GMAIL_UPDATE_LABEL] Field naming/shape can be strict (e.g., user_id vs userId), causing validation failures if mismatched."], "reference_workbench_snippets": [{"description": "Extract labels robustly from direct or wrapped outputs", "code": "```python
