{"data": {"results": [{"index": 1, "use_case": "Please use gmail to permanently delete that message for me.", "execution_guidance": "IMPORTANT: Follow the recommended plan below. Extract steps before execution, adapt to your current context, execute sequentially with current_step parameter, and check known pitfalls to avoid errors.", "recommended_plan_steps": ["[Required] [Prerequisite]: Define exact deletion scope (search query/labels/categories; include_spam_trash; message vs thread; trash vs permanent) before any discovery using GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS (avoid wrong targeting).", "[Required (if messageIds unknown)] [Step]: Discover candidate IDs using GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS (prefer ids_only=true); paginate nextPageToken→page_token, merge+dedupe IDs across pages/queries.", "[Optional (if large runs/resumable checkpoints needed)] [Step]: Use COMPOSIO_REMOTE_WORKBENCH to persist/dedupe IDs and build deterministic ≤1000-sized chunks for repeatable execution.", "[Optional (for safety before destructive actions)] [Next Step]: Spot-check a small sample using GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_MESSAGE_ID (confirm scope matches intent).", "[Optional (if staging/review is desired)] [Next Step]: Resolve label IDs via GMAIL_LIST_LABELS, then apply/remove a temporary review label using GMAIL_BATCH_MODIFY_MESSAGES (quarantine/approve set before deletion).", "[Required] [Prerequisite]: Get explicit confirmation of final scope, deduped match count, and chosen delete_type before any write using GMAIL_BATCH_DELETE_MESSAGES or GMAIL_MOVE_TO_TRASH.", "[Required] [Step]: If trash chosen, use GMAIL_MOVE_TO_TRASH (or GMAIL_MOVE_THREAD_TO_TRASH for thread scope); if permanent chosen, use GMAIL_BATCH_DELETE_MESSAGES in ≤1000 IDs per call (or GMAIL_DELETE_THREAD for thread scope) with backoff on 429/5xx, then verify by re-running GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS (expect 0 matches).", "[Fallback (if permanent delete fails or reversible cleanup is preferred)] [Fallback]: Use GMAIL_MOVE_TO_TRASH (or GMAIL_MOVE_THREAD_TO_TRASH); recover mistaken trash with GMAIL_UNTRASH_MESSAGE."], "known_pitfalls": ["[GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS] nextPageToken can be an empty string; treat any falsy token as end-of-pagination even if messages are returned.", "[GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS] page_token must come from a prior nextPageToken; arbitrary tokens can raise "Invalid pageToken" or skip results.", "[GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS] Responses may be wrapped (data/results variants); extract messages and nextPageToken defensively when collecting IDs.", "[GMAIL_BATCH_DELETE_MESSAGES] Max 1000 messageIds per call; the API may accept a batch while silently skipping invalid/already-deleted IDs, so verify via GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS.", "[GMAIL_LIST_LABELS] GMAIL_BATCH_MODIFY_MESSAGES requires internal label IDs, not display names."], "reference_workbench_snippets": [{"description": "Paginate GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS (ids_only) across variable response shapes and collect/dedupe messageId until nextPageToken is missing/empty", "code": "```python
message_ids=[]; token=None
while True:
  p={"user_id":"user","max_results":500,"ids_only":True}
  if token: p["page_token"]=token
  r,e=run_composio_tool("GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS",p)
  if e: raise Exception(e)
  d=(r or {}).get("data",{})
  if "results" in (r or {}): d=((r["results"][0].get("response") or {}).get("data") or d)
  d=d.get("data",d)
  for m in (d.get("messages") or []):
    mid=m.get("messageId")
    if mid: message_ids.append(mid)
  token=d.get("nextPageToken")
  if not token: break
message_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(message_ids))
```"}, {"description": "Delete messageIds in ≤1000-sized chunks via GMAIL_BATCH_DELETE_MESSAGES", "code": "```python
