{"data": {"results": [{"index": 1, "use_case": "Download the attachment from my gmail message.", "execution_guidance": "IMPORTANT: Follow the recommended plan below. Extract steps before execution, adapt to your current context, execute sequentially with current_step parameter, and check known pitfalls to avoid errors.", "recommended_plan_steps": ["[Required] [Prerequisite]: Discover candidate emails using GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS (query like has:attachment + sender/subject/keywords/date; paginate with nextPageToken until missing or ""; treat messages=[] as valid no-match; use messages[].messageId and threadId; pick newest if needed).", "[Optional (if GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS returns insufficient matches)] [Prerequisite]: Broaden discovery using GMAIL_LIST_THREADS (enumerate likely threads, then use threadId for targeted hydration).", "[Required] [Prerequisite]: Hydrate authoritative attachment metadata using GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_MESSAGE_ID (format="full"; prefer data.attachmentList (attachmentId, filename, mimeType); otherwise walk data.payload.parts recursively to collect (attachmentId,file_name) pairs).", "[Required] [Step]: Filter to target attachment(s) (exclude inline/signature assets; match filename/mimeType/context) and keep paired (message_id, attachment_id, file_name) from the same attachment entry.", "[Required] [Step]: Download each chosen file using GMAIL_GET_ATTACHMENT (message_id + attachment_id + file_name) and capture response.data.file.name, response.data.file.mimetype, response.data.file.s3url.", "[Optional (if GMAIL_GET_ATTACHMENT fails with 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT/"Invalid attachment token", s3url expired/invalid, or attachment is on another message)] [Fallback]: Use GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_THREAD_ID to scan messages, then re-run GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_MESSAGE_ID (format="full") to refresh identifiers and retry GMAIL_GET_ATTACHMENT (re-calling also re-mints a fresh file.s3url).", "[Optional (if you must fetch/parse bytes promptly or at scale)] [Next Step]: Use COMPOSIO_REMOTE_WORKBENCH to download response.data.file.s3url before expiry and checkpoint per attachment for resume/retry.", "[Optional (after successful downloads and explicit user confirmation; write operation)] [Next Step]: Mark processed messages using GMAIL_BATCH_MODIFY_MESSAGES (e.g., remove UNREAD/apply processed label) to prevent reprocessing."], "known_pitfalls": ["[GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS] Paginate with nextPageToken; stop when token is missing OR empty string; results use messages[].messageId (not messages[].id) and messages=[] can be a valid no-match.", "[GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_MESSAGE_ID] Use format="full"; attachmentId may require walking nested data.payload.parts[].parts; UI/previews can truncate long attachmentId strings so use full response fields.", "[GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_MESSAGE_ID] HTTP 404 NOT_FOUND can mean the messageId isn’t in the connected mailbox scope; re-discover via GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS or GMAIL_LIST_THREADS instead of retrying blindly.", "[GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_THREAD_ID] May fail with HTTP 403 PERMISSION_DENIED "insufficient authentication scopes" if the Gmail connection lacks thread-read scopes.", "[GMAIL_GET_ATTACHMENT] file_name is required; 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT "Invalid attachment token" indicates wrong/stale attachmentId; response.data.file.s3url is presigned (observed X-Amz-Expires=3600) and can break if copied HTML-escaped (e.g., '&amp;')—download promptly or re-mint by calling GMAIL_GET_ATTACHMENT again."], "reference_workbench_snippets": [{"description": "Parse hydrated Gmail message payload parts to collect (filename, attachmentId) pairs", "code": "```python
def walk(parts,out):
